A||N||9||jaguiler||Air Conditioning..... how cold....?||||5||
Z||000000||jaguiler||04-27-2001||03:56 PM||||Hello,<P>It is starting to get hot over here.... I charged my compressor today with r134.... my car has been converted.  Now the AC works but it seems like the air it is pushing out is not that cold...  <BR>My friend has a Cavalier I charged his as well and he has the same problem.....<BR>As far as I know all parts are fine in my car and functional.... belt is fine with no slack.....  what could this be?<P>------------------<BR>______<BR>__|aguiler||65.8.46.102||reg||5
Z||000001||jaguiler||04-27-2001||04:30 PM||||BTW - I check to see if my compressor turns while the car is off... chking to see if clutch works.  When car is on and the AC on the clutch is engages and spinning the belt.... so i know my parts are not frozen.....<P>Thanks in advance!<P>------------------<BR>______<BR>__|aguiler||65.8.46.102||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||04-27-2001||07:27 PM||||could be a number of things. undercharged. broken interior controls. those are good items to check.||||reg||1
